%% ============================================================
\chapter{Discussion}
%% ============================================================

\textit{This chapter will discuss all findings in relation to the research questions and existing literature after results are collected. The structure below defines what each section must address.}

\section{Discussion of \sq{1} --- The VM Failure Threshold}

This section will discuss the measured failure threshold against resource contention theory from Pillar 1. It will address whether the collapse was non-linear as predicted and at what concurrency level it occurred. It will also discuss whether the result was surprising and what it implies for teams currently running similar workloads on a \vm{}.

\section{Discussion of \sq{2} --- Pod Isolation Effectiveness}

This section will evaluate whether pod isolation delivered the theoretical blast radius reduction predicted by distributed systems fault isolation theory (Pillar 4). It will compare execution time variance between \vm{} and \gke{} and discuss whether the isolation held under deliberate failure conditions.

\section{Discussion of \sq{3} --- Autoscaling Response}

This section will discuss the measured autoscaling response window against the autoscaling latency literature from Pillar 3. It will evaluate whether the response time makes \gke{} viable under spike conditions and what job-level impact was observed during the scale-out gap.

\section{Discussion of \sq{4} --- The Crossover Point}

This section will present and interpret the primary contribution --- the formally defined crossover point. It will discuss at what concurrency level the point was found, what it means for engineering migration decisions, and how it relates to Kubernetes overhead literature from Pillar 2. It will also address whether the result was surprising or consistent with theoretical predictions.

\section{Discussion of \sq{5} --- Infrastructure Reproducibility}

This section will evaluate the reproducibility of the \cdktf{} and Helm setup and discuss any deviations observed across rebuild cycles and their potential impact on experimental validity.

\section{Trade-off Analysis}

This section will synthesise all five research question discussions into a balanced trade-off analysis: what the \gke{} migration improves, what it costs, and under what conditions each architecture is more appropriate. This section answers the main research question directly.

\section{Limitations}

\begin{itemize}
  \item Environments are not identical --- treated as part of the behavioral comparison, not eliminated
  \item \textsc{gcp} free tier resource constraints may affect results --- documented as a research variable
  \item Synthetic workloads --- may not capture all real-world pipeline behavior patterns
  \item Single cloud provider --- results directionally relevant but may not generalize to all platforms
  \item \dagster{} as representative system --- other workflow frameworks may behave differently
\end{itemize}

